From cd8d6fa1513e3777c3b566bde6b4595fc7e79a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrianProk <Prokopczyk.Adrian@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:10:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] DIRECTOR: Initialize the scale of digital video cast
 members read from a cast

Commit 6c8a0e45f1 added _scaleX/_scaleY and made getInitialRect()
multiply the video size with them, but only the default constructor
sets them to 100. The constructor that reads the member from cast data
left them uninitialized, so sprites of these videos got a random size:
640x480 when the leftover value happened to be 0 or 100, otherwise
e.g. 13030x480 or 13100x23424.

The widget is created at the sprite size and the frame is stretched
into it for every frame. On the desktop this went mostly unnoticed. On
the 3DS (The Great Green Mouse Disaster) it made some videos play at
2 fps with heap peaks of 65 MB, and the oversized allocations
eventually froze the game after a number of rooms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp b/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp
index 23fd2fd11d..63a3f94a30 100644
--- a/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp
@@ -145,6 +145,9 @@ DigitalVideoCastMember::DigitalVideoCastMember(Cast *cast, uint16 castId, Common
 	_center = _vflags & 0x01;
 	_dirty = false;
 	_emptyFile = false;
+	// The scale is a D7 property that is not stored in the cast data read here;
+	// getInitialRect() multiplies the video size with it
+	_scaleX = _scaleY = 100;
 
 	memset(_ditheringPalette, 0, 256*3);
 
